@xiezhq-hermann could you review this? It is a smaller version of #31713, which you are assigned on, and it touches the unified radix cache and the SWA allocator path.

@jellysnack this reuses your replay-length formula and gain threshold from #31713. Could you check that it covers what you need, and say if you would rather land yours?

cc @hnyls2002 for the scheduler and batch changes.

CI needs the `run-ci` label.

I merged main at `c891c5c7ca` to clear a conflict with #43166 (encoder replay folded into the extend). The conflicts were only where both changes added lines next to each other, so the rebuild code itself did not change.

The DSpark rebuild row was run again after the merge: 8/8 hits, average KL 0.0030, 0.24 s after eviction against 2.21 s cold, and no scheduler exceptions. The details are in the PR description.

@xiezhq-hermann @hnyls2002 could one of you take a first look when you have time? The branch has no conflicts with main, and it still needs the `run-ci` label.

